  "title": "dfilter: Don't crash on arithmetic between string literals",
  "description": "Don't assert that we can't get to the arithmetic check with\na string literal node.\n\nInstead of:\n\n./run/dftest -s 'http.host == \"host\" + \".com\"'\nFilter:\n http.host == \"host\" + \".com\"\n\n ** (dftest:389225) 19:51:58.295340 [DFilter ERROR] epan/dfilter/semcheck.c:2078 -- check_arithmetic(): Invalid syntax node type 'STRING'.\n ** (dftest:389225) Aborting on fatal log level exception\nAborted (core dumped)\n\n$ ./run/dftest -s 'http.host == \"host\" + \".com\"'\nFilter:\n http.host == \"host\" + \".com\"\n\nError: FT_STRING cannot be added.\n  http.host == \"host\" + \".com\"\n\nPerhaps in the future we could support the addition operator with\nstring, to mean concatenation?",
